# Daromadchi scheduled jobs — install with `crontab scripts/crontab.example`
# AFTER reconciling with the live crontab. See docs/ops/cron.md.
#
# ⚠️  ONLY ONE LINE HERE IS KNOWN-CORRECT.
#
# The live schedule has never been in version control, so this file cannot be a
# copy of it. `expire-plans` is documented in docs/plans/turnover-pricing-spec.md
# and is reproduced exactly. Every other cadence below is a PROPOSAL derived from
# what the code implies, and must be checked against `crontab -l` on the VPS
# before it replaces anything — see docs/ops/cron.md for the diff procedure.
#
# Overwriting the live crontab with these guesses would silently change how often
# sellers' data syncs and when they are charged. Reconcile first.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
DAROMADCHI_DIR=/var/www/daromadchi
DAROMADCHI_URL=https://www.daromadchi.uz
MAILTO=""

# ── KNOWN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Daily housekeeping, and the busiest job in the product: it expires lapsed
# plans, recomputes every derived tier, sends due price notices, runs the
# free-tier nudges, and steps the account-lifecycle ladder. Documented at
# docs/plans/turnover-pricing-spec.md §3.
15 3 * * *   /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh expire-plans

# ── PROPOSED — verify against `crontab -l` before use ─────────────────────────

# Marketplace order/product sync. The landing page tells sellers orders update
# "every 15 minutes", and lib/uzum/sync.ts calls the cron "half-hourly" — those
# two disagree, so the live value decides.
*/15 * * * *  /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh sync

# Stock write-back. Frequency is a trade-off nobody has written down: too slow
# oversells, too fast burns marketplace rate limit.
*/10 * * * *  /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh stock-sync

# Telegram digests. The route filters on each seller's own notification window
# (lib/telegram.ts isInNotificationWindow), so this only needs to run often
# enough that no window is missed — hourly at :05 clears the hour boundary.
5 * * * *     /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh telegram-digest

# Renewals. Charges cards, so it runs once a day and early, leaving the working
# day for a human to see failures. Gated by BILLING_AUTORENEW_ENABLED — with that
# unset this is a no-op regardless of schedule.
30 2 * * *    /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh billing-renew
